<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Omar Torrijos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1929–1981</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Omar Torrijos was a Panamanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a> officer who became the country's leader after the coup of 1968 and dominated its politics until his death in a plane crash in 1981. He negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torrijos-carter-treaties">Torrijos–Carter Treaties</a> of 1977 with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, which provided for Panama to take full control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> at the end of 1999.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omar-torrijos.jpg" alt="Omar Torrijos" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: President (1977-1981 : Carter). White House Staff Photographers. (01/20/1977 - 01/20/1981) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Omar_Torrijos_1978.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
